---
term: Power balancing
section: coordination
order: 40
definition: A parent corporation's active correction of power imbalances among its constituents in pursuit of its own higher-order common interest.
seeAlso:
  - arbitration
---
Representation doesn't mean influence proportional to wealth, membership, or institutional capacity. The parent is an active arbitrator, not a passive federation. The aim isn't necessarily equality. It's preventing lower-level power asymmetries from undermining the parent's charter.
